          body: "Expect the angles (15, 45, 90), the sites by age (vastus lateralis for the infant, ventrogluteal for the adult, deltoid for a 0.5 mL vaccine in a schoolchild), the volumes (1 mL deltoid, 3 mL ventrogluteal), the bleb (no bleb — invalid, repeat), and the Mantoux reading (induration at 48–72 hours). Expect the spacer question (one puff, five breaths, thirty seconds between), the ear question (up and back over three, down and back under), the eye question (lower sac, punctal occlusion, drops before ointment), the sublingual question (do not swallow) and the fentanyl patch question (no heat, fold and dispose, write the date). Expect the controlled-drug question in the form of a discrepancy at handover (report now, do not alter the register) and the error question in the form of ‘what should the nurse do first’ (assess the patient).",
